    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24557" root="صقب" body-key="S">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَصْقَبَتْ دَارُهُ</span></b> : see 1, second sentence. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اصقبهُ</span> <i>He made him,</i> or <i>it, to be near.</i> (S, K.)
And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اصقب ٱللّٰهُ دَارَهُ</span> <i>May God make his house to
be near.</i> (A.) [And so with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">س</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And one
says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَصْقَبَكَ الصَّيْدُ</span> <i>The game,</i> or <i>object of the
chase, has become near to thee, so that thou art
able to shoot,</i> or <i>cast, at it.</i> (K.)

